+### Why the earlier port was replaced
+
+The 16 dev runs of 2026-09-10/11 (`data/rudin_*`, task `QuadrupedPD-v0`) were a
+partial port: 100 Hz, SB3 instead of `rsl_rl`, a hand-tuned default pose, and —
+decisively — termination at this project's z-band floor of 0.20 m. Under the
+recipe's zero action the Kp = 20 PD sags the body to **0.218 m mean, 0.188 m
+min** (measured, `examples/tests/unitree_recipe_check.py`), so that floor
+terminated the recipe's own default stance. `legged_gym` terminates on base
+contact instead. Those runs are dev artefacts, not results.
+
+### Disturbance for the first trial
+
+The recipe's only external disturbance is `legged_gym`'s `push_robots`
+(`LeggedRobotCfg.domain_rand`, inherited by Go2): the base's world x/y velocity
+is overwritten with U(−1, 1) m/s every 750 policy steps (15 s) and — because
+`_push_robots` runs after `reset_idx` with `episode_length_buf == 0` — on every
+reset except the first. **It is on.** This project's impulse sampler is not part
+of the recipe and is **off** (`external_force_enable = false`).
+
+### What is reproduced exactly
+
+| aspect | recipe | here |
+|---|---|---|
+| policy rate / decimation | 50 Hz; target held, PD re-evaluated each physics step | 50 Hz (`frame_skip` 10 × 2 ms, asserted by the env); PD re-evaluated each 1 ms physics step |
+| PD law, clip | `clip(Kp(a·0.25 + q₀ − q) − Kd·q̇, ±effort)`, Kp 20, Kd 0.5 | same; clip by MuJoCo actuator force range at every physics step, leg-controller clamp lifted so no feedforward residual |
