+# Status — RL-only baseline implementation
+
+**Updated:** 2026-09-11
+**Plan:** `docs/RL_ONLY_BASELINE_PLAN.md` — read its "2026-09-11 revision"
+**Branches:** `rl-only-baseline` in `envpool` and `quadcontrol` (uncommitted)
+**State:** Workstreams A–D implemented. The `rudin` arm is an exact recreation
+of `unitree_rl_gym`'s Go2 task (`QuadrupedPD-v1`, vendored `rsl_rl` v1.0.2).
+Deterministic recipe checks pass. No trial run yet. E (runs) and F (evaluation
+integration, which needs an `rsl_rl` checkpoint loader) remain.
+
+## 2026-09-11 — what went wrong with the first port, and what replaced it
+
+Sixteen dev runs (`data/rudin_smoke*`, `data/rudin_flat*`, task
+`QuadrupedPD-v0`, SB3) produced no usable arm. Causes, from their manifests,
+TensorBoard logs and surviving console logs:
+
+- **Judged too early.** 5M steps is 51 PPO iterations of the recipe's 1500
+  (3.4 %). The "stable gait at 5M" gate came from Gamma, whose policy starts on
+  top of a walking WBIC with std 0.05; this arm starts from std 1.0.
+- **Smoke gate overridden five times.** Smokes v1–v5 had 20–105-step episodes
+  (the robot never stood), and a 5M run followed each.
+- **A change that never reached training.** v3 and v4 are identical to the digit
+  despite different simulator binaries.
+- **No provenance.** Seven simulator binaries across sixteen runs, nothing
+  committed, console logs written to container `/tmp` and overwritten; why v5
+  stopped at 1.08M is unknowable.
+- **Termination at the 0.20 m evaluation floor** — a height constraint the
+  recipe's reward never prices (its `base_height` scale is 0). The recipe's own
+  zero-action stance sags to 0.218 m mean, 0.188 m min.
+- **Undeclared recipe changes:** v8 narrowed commands to vx only; the default
+  pose was hand-tuned; a 0.05 std floor was added.
+
+Replacement (this revision):
+
+| piece | where |
+|---|---|
+| exact task | `envpool/envpool/mujoco/gym/quadruped_wbc.h`, joint-PD branch (`InitJointPD`, `ResetJointPD`, `StepJointPD`, `ComputeJointPDReward`); registered as `QuadrupedPD-v1` (`frame_skip` 10, `max_episode_steps` 1001). `QuadrupedPD-v0` is gone. |
+| simulator access | `SimRobotState` + get/set state, base-velocity push, friction, actuator force limits, base contact force: `MdlSimDriver`, `SimHW`, `RLPipelineRuntime` |
+| arm config | `config/robots/sim/envpool_train_rudin.toml` — our impulse sampler off, leg-controller clamp lifted, Unitree default pose mapped, command sampler off |
+| algorithm | `envpool/examples/third_party/rsl_rl` (v1.0.2, unmodified, `SHA256SUMS`) |
+| adapter / trainer | `envpool/examples/common/rsl_vec_env.py`, `envpool/examples/train_unitree.py` (refuses to overwrite a run dir; writes both repos' HEAD + diffs, `.so` hash, full config before step 1) |
+| smoke gate | `envpool/examples/tests/unitree_recipe_check.py` — deterministic, no PPO |
+| retired | `examples/train.py --recipe unitree` now exits and points to the new trainer |
+
+### Recipe checks (64 envs) — all pass
+
+obs/action dims 48/12 · reset base height 0.42 · policy dt 0.020 s ·
+commands zeroed below 0.2 and within ±1, yaw command within ±1 · saturated
+torque term −0.03819 = the value for 23.7/23.7/35.55 N·m limits (100 % of envs) ·
+zero-action stand: 64/64 reach the 20 s timeout at step 1001, 0 early
+terminations, mean base height 0.218 m · observation noise within
+`_get_noise_scale_vec` bounds.
+
+### Launching a trial
+
+Inside the container, one run per directory, console inside it:
+
+```bash
+RUN=data/rudin_unitree/trial1_seed1
+mkdir -p $RUN && python3 examples/train_unitree.py --run-dir $RUN > $RUN/console.log 2>&1
+```
+
+Judge a trial on the full 1500 iterations (plus `final_eval.py` once F exists),
+not on an early slice.
+
+## 2026-09-10 — Workstream A (record)
+
+- Renamed the custom Gym `humanoid.h` to `quadruped_wbc.h`, including bindings,
+  registration, examples, and live evaluation references. Real Gym
+  `HumanoidStandup` and DeepMind Control Humanoid remain untouched.
+- One class, `privileged_observations` configuration switch: `QuadrupedWBC-v0`
+  emits 54 observations and `QuadrupedWBC-v1` emits 61. This follows the existing
+  Ant configuration idiom instead of introducing the planned templated classes.
+- The first 54 writes share one bounded `FillObservation` implementation.
+  The earlier review against `0fd79b7` found only additive changes for the
+  privileged tail and force-overlay/telemetry plumbing, with no changes to
+  reward, action, physics, or the first 54 writes.
+- Evaluation chooses the task from checkpoint width before loading normalization.
+  Gamma and Delta checkpoints use their native task; the adapter remains only
+  as the existing fallback for other widths.
+- The parity check now fails for a missing renamed header when the sibling
+  envpool checkout is present instead of silently skipping it.
+- Removed the obsolete Gym Humanoid alignment and determinism cases. The latter
+  was missed in the original handoff: it still requested removed `Humanoid-v4`
+  and creates three simultaneous pools with uncontrolled custom-runtime RNGs.
+  The dedicated controlled split regression is `evaluations/wbc_split_gate.py`.
+
+## Controlled regression result
+
+Checkpoint: `gamma5_stage3/quadruped_ppo_model_ckpt_4000256.zip`, with its matching
+VecNormalize file. The existing vectorized evaluator ran serial processes for
+native v0 and v1 with the 54-column adapter. No production task mapping was
+edited to force the comparison; the adapter variant overrides the mapping only
+inside its own diagnostic process.
+
+Protocol: forward 47.46 N·s (237.3 N for 0.2 s), body frame latched at onset,
+nominal initialization, fixed command 0.8 m/s, random onset phase after three
+gait cycles, common 5.5 s recovery window. Two batches of 64 episodes per path.
+The shared simulator lock was held. No WBIC evaluations or training ran.
+
+| Seed | Native v0 survivors | v1 + adapter survivors | Paired outcome differences |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| 4242 | 32/64 | 32/64 | 0 |
+| 14242 | 24/64 | 24/64 | 0 |
+
+**All 128 pairs also had exactly equal onset times and total rewards.** All
+surviving episodes passed force-delivery integration and scoring-window checks.
+These are regression results for one challenging cell, not a six-direction
+J50 estimate or statistical proof of equivalence across all conditions.
+
+Artifacts (local, results are git-ignored):
+`evaluations/results/20260910_wbc_split_gate/`, containing `report.json`, all
+four `summary.csv` and `force_audit.json` files, evaluator logs, build logs,
+and the exact launch script `run_gate.py`.
+
+Reproduce in a new output directory from the host:
+
+```bash
+python3 evaluations/wbc_split_gate.py --run-dir wbc_split_gate_repeat
+```
+
+The maintained script additionally records checkpoint and normalization hashes
+and writes a paired comparison report, failing on any survival/onset/reward
+difference. Differences call for investigation, not automatic attribution to
+the observation split.
+
+## Correction to the earlier reproducibility finding
+
+The handoff reported max first-54-column differences of 8.54 across v0/v1 and
+18.72 across two v0 processes, beginning at reset. That uncontrolled probe did
+not establish that fully specified seeds fail to reproduce the runtime.
+
+`envpool.toml` enables command randomization with `policy_random_seed = -1`.
+`MdlRLCommandSource` seeds that RNG using `std::random_device`, independently of
+EnvPool's seed. Thus setting only the EnvPool seed leaves a source of entropy.
+The controlled evaluator explicitly disables command randomization, and its
+paired metrics matched exactly. This identifies a confound in the earlier
+probe, not a complete investigation of every source of nondeterminism. Training
+with entropy-seeded commands is not made replayable by setting EnvPool's seed
+alone; training RNG plumbing was not changed in this workstream.
+
+## Validation and unresolved runtime failure
+
+- Host `python3 -m pytest evaluations/tests/test_parameter_parity.py -q`:
+  **47 passed**.
+- `make run` in the existing `envpool-dev` container: first attempt built and
+  installed the wheel, then the 5,000-step `examples/env_step.py` aborted after
+  several resets with **`double free or corruption (fasttop)`**, exit 134
+  (make exit 2). See `build.log`.
+- An unchanged repeat of `make run` **passed, exit 0**, total execution 18 s.
+  See `build_retry.log`. A passing retry does not resolve the intermittent abort.
+- All four checkpoint-evaluation processes completed successfully.
+- Full host evaluation-test collection is blocked by an existing missing
+  `autotune.core.storage` import in `test_run_lock.py`; no dependency installs
+  or unrelated autotune changes were made.
+- The initial diagnostic command used Docker's `/app` cwd, which shadowed the
+  installed package with a source import and failed on `jaraco`. Launching in
+  `/app/quadcontrol` after the sanctioned `make run` resolved that import path.
+
+The heap-corruption cause is **unknown**. Do not label it fixed, attribute it to
+the rename without evidence, or hide it by shortening the normal build example.
+Before B, isolate the repeated-reset/logging crash so later pipeline changes do
+not obscure its origin. Then implement `MdlRLJointPD`, explicitly zero the absent
+cached gait schedule and derive the default pose from our simulator config.
+
+`msc-thesis` remains on `master` with its pre-existing `agents.md` path correction;
+this continuation did not modify or commit that repository.
